WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:03.560
Are you self-employed?

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.830
Freelancing?

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:12.250
Do you have a side hustle?

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:16.139
All of these are various types of independent
contracting and together they are part of

00:00:16.139 --> 00:00:18.250
what has become known as the gig economy.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:23.609
Three in 10 Americans do gig work of some
kind or another.

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:26.820
And for many freelancing is synonymous with
freedom.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:27.829
But freedom isn't free.

00:00:27.829 --> 00:00:30.759
There's a lot of instability that comes with
the gig economy.

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:32.669
It's a hustle, its a grind.

00:00:32.669 --> 00:00:35.990
You don't have that safety net of a salary
and jobs.

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:38.520
Basically working from paycheck to paycheck.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:46.830
This is good money and we are going to help
you run the business of you.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:51.300
OK so the gig economy is a broad topic so
let's separate it into two sections.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.830
There's the career freelancer and the side
hustler.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:57.440
Let's start with side hustling because I'm
a humble video producer and I could use some

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:58.440
extra scratch.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:01.050
But will I get in trouble with my company
for doing that?

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:05.830
I wish there was somebody I could talk to
about this.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:06.960
Hey.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.329
I can help you out with this.

00:01:08.329 --> 00:01:09.329
Who are you?

00:01:09.329 --> 00:01:12.700
My name's Mark Koehler I'm just sitting over
here read my own book on the very topic you're

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.700
talking about.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:14.700
Oh who let you in the building?

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:15.700
Well I'm here for an interview.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:16.700
Oh.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.700
Oh my gosh.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:18.700
Wow.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:19.700
So let's get started.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:20.700
Will I get in trouble with my company if I
want to start a side hustle?

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.920
Generally not unless you're gonna try to start
a small business in your industry.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.369
Nine times out of ten you're gonna be fine.

00:01:25.369 --> 00:01:31.969
You go out do whatever you want.

00:01:31.969 --> 00:01:34.530
Once you are a side hustler you're basically
a small business.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:38.530
Yeah a lot of people don't realize if I'm
just even driving for Uber you're getting

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:39.810
a ten ninety nine baby.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:40.810
That's a small business.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:44.740
Let's take advantage of it and the tax write
offs could be phenomenal.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:45.740
Tell me about that.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:50.869
Well under the new Tax Cuts and Jobs Act we've
got what's called a 20 percent pass through.

00:01:50.869 --> 00:02:01.520
We've got cell phone, home office computers
electronics, travel, auto all these little

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.619
things that you might be paying for anyway.

00:02:03.619 --> 00:02:05.630
I call it personal conversion expenses.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:10.920
So what happens if my side hustle becomes
so successful that it's cutting into all my

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:11.920
time?

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:12.920
Well congratulations.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:16.459
Now you graduated to career freelancer your
full time business owner.

00:02:16.459 --> 00:02:23.209
It's better to quit your job now and make
more money at home.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:31.430
You know what, I Quit!

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:32.760
Wait a second.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.510
Was that a good idea?

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:40.049
What about my vacation time, my 401K, my health
insurance and that discounted gym membership

00:02:40.049 --> 00:02:42.299
I never signed up for?

00:02:42.299 --> 00:02:45.709
Freelancing seems like a lot more work than
a real job- mostly because you have to do

00:02:45.709 --> 00:02:51.760
everything yourself.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.150
What better place to see advice than the Freelancers
Union?

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.540
So let’s head to their HQ and talk to Caitlin
Pearce.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.370
Caitlin thank you so much for having me.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:00.370
My pleasure.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.379
Let's say I just became a career freelancer.

00:03:02.379 --> 00:03:06.650
What can I do to feel as secure as I did as
a staffer?

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.980
You know when people are thinking about whether
or not to become a freelancer I always say

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.310
before you make that leap think about a couple
of things.

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:17.819
One is you know what is your plan for earning
enough income not just to support yourself

00:03:17.819 --> 00:03:22.689
but also to take on the additional costs of
managing your tax burden paying for your own

00:03:22.689 --> 00:03:27.200
health benefits and having a savings plan
for retirement.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.939
Should I be hiring somebody to do my taxes
for me?

00:03:30.939 --> 00:03:32.260
Short answer yes.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:36.930
One of the things all freelancers need especially
if they're doing this full time is someone

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:41.030
they can help you understand what you can
deduct for your business and make sure that

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:45.079
you've done your taxes properly so you don't
end up with a liability at the end of the

00:03:45.079 --> 00:03:46.079
year.

00:03:46.079 --> 00:03:50.359
Could you give me a few financial tips for
freelancers to feel more secure?

00:03:50.359 --> 00:03:55.849
First of all every freelancer needs to have
a good contract that they've worked with a

00:03:55.849 --> 00:03:59.239
lawyer and that they understand that's going
to protect their work and make sure they get

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.469
paid on time.

00:04:00.469 --> 00:04:06.439
Secondly you should have a system by which
you are automatically setting aside 30 percent

00:04:06.439 --> 00:04:11.219
of your income into taxes as soon as it comes
in before you can touch it.

00:04:11.219 --> 00:04:16.180
And if you can also setting aside income in
the short term and long term savings.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:20.250
The third thing I think is that you should
really set aside 10 percent of your time for

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:26.280
long term planning and that should include
business building activities like client prospecting

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.750
networking investing in training or up-skilling.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:34.190
And it's really important for you to have
a vision for where you're going.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:38.720
Think about where you want to be in five years
financially and professionally and be making

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:42.280
steps towards working towards those goals.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.220
So that should get all you freelancers inside
hustlers off on the right foot.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.220
As for me.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.499
I'm going to beg for my cushy staff job back.

